\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces In the Plot it is represented the plot for $\ee ^{- \lambda (\cosh (x)-1)}$ and an increasing $\lambda = 1, 2, 10, 70$ - darker represent larger values of the parameter. The dotted patter represents $\ee ^{-\lambda x^2}$ for large lambda.}}{27}{figure.caption.14}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The lines represent the solution to $\mathop {\textrm Im}[f(z) - f(t_c)] = 0$ for the three possible cases of the Hermite Polynomial. These are the curves we use to perform the asymptotic analysis on the integral. Note the case $\alpha = 2$; the coalescence of critical point gives origin to the Airy function.}}{39}{figure.caption.15}%
